  "raw_text": "252\n\nSaura tawaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto turn bad, to become bad, to become corrupt\n \n/ volverse malo, volverse corrupto\n\nTnaya ra tawaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nTnayara tawaia, Tnayara tauaia\n,\n \nNayara tawaia\n,\n \nNayara tauaia\n,\n \nSnayara tawaia\n,\n \nSnayara\ntauaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto turn to the side, to turn aside, to turn away, to stray, to stray from the good\n \n/ volverse a un lado,\napartarse, alejarse, alejarse del bien\n\nTânka kasak wina tnaya ra tawan nani\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npeople who turned away from the truth\n \n/ personas que\nalejaron de la verdad\n\nTawan\n \n(v\n-\n3p\n-\npast\n/pasado\n)\n \n–\n \nturned, changed direction, returned\n \n/\n \ndio vuelta, cambió de dirección, regresó\n\nTawan\n \n(a/t:\n \nTaun\n-\nbh,my,sp\n;\n \nTauwan\n-\ndict\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ntown, village, city, community\n \n/ pueblo, ciudad, comunidad\n\n(Construct:\n \nTawanki\n \n–\n \nmy town\n \n/ mi ciudad;\n \nTawankam\n \n–\n \nyour town\n \n/ tu ciudad;\n \nTawanka\n \n–\n \nhis/her/its/their town\n \n/ su ciudad)\n\n(Construct forms of former spelling / Formas constructivas de ortografía anterior:\n \nTaunki\n \n–\n \nmy town\n... / mi ciudad\n…\n \n;\n \nTaunkam\n \n–\n\nyour town\n... / tu ciudad\n…\n;\n \nTaunka\n \n–\n \nhis/her/their town\n... / su ciudad\n…\n)\n\nTawan almukka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ntown\n/city/village\n \nelder\n \n/ pueblo/ciudad anciano\n\nTa\nwan\n \ndimaika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ntown\n \nentrance, city entrance\n \n/ entrada de la ciudad\n\nTawan luhpika kum kaia\n \n(\nwqu-08/19\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto be a citizen\n \n/ ser ciudadano\n\n“Tawan pranakira ba”\n \n(\nwqu-05/20-Daniel 11:41\n)\n \n–\n \n“the land of the Decoration”\n \n/\n \n“la Tierra Hermosa”\n\nTawan tara\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbig town\n/city\n \n/ gran pueblo/ciudad\n\nTawan uplika nani\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ntownspeople, villagers\n \n/ gente del pueblo, aldeanos\n\nTawan wihtka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ntown/city/village ruler, town/city/village judge, town/city/village head\n, secular authority\n \n/\n\ngobernante de pueblo/ciudad, juez de pueblo/ciudad, jefe de pueblo/ciudad, autoridad secular\n\nYukuwaika tawanka\n \n(a/t:\n \nYukuwaia tawanka ba\n)\n \n–\n \ncity of refuge\n \n/ ciudad de refugio\n\nTâwan\n \n(Tawan)\n \n(n/s,adv)\n \n–\n \nsake, reason, for the sake of, for the reason of, because of\n \n/ motivo, por el bien de, por la razon\nde, por causa de\n\n(Construct:\n \nTâiwan\n \n(Taiwan)\n;\n \nTâmwan\n \n(Tamwan)\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb31\n):\n \nYawan nu sa Jehova Gâdkam ba tâmwan aiklabisa.\n \n–\n \nWe know that your God Jehovah fights for you.\n \n/ Sabemos que\ntu Dios Jehová lucha por ti.)\n\n(\nEx/Ej(\nlfb46\n):\n \nElías Acab ra win ai saurka tâwan, Israel ra lî auhbia apia\n \n–\n \nElijah told Ahab that because of his badness, it would not\nrain in Israel\n \n/ Elías le dijo a Acab que debido a su maldad, no llovería en Israel)\n\nDîa tâwan?\n \n–\n \nWhy?, What caused this?, For what reason?\n \n/ ¿Por qué?, ¿Qué causó esto?, ¿Por qué motivo?\n\nTâwan daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto do because of, to make because of, to do for the sake of, to make for the sake of\n \n/ hacer\npor, hacer por el bien de\n\nTâwan aisaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto speak up for, to speak for the sake of\n \n/ hablar por, hablar por el bien de\n\n(\nEx/Ej(\nwqu-09/20\n):\n \nJisas nahki Meri t\nȃ\nwan aisan?\n \n–\n \nHow did Jesus speak up for (defend) Mary?\n \n/ ¿Cómo habló Jesús por\n(defendiendo) a María?)\n\nTawar\n \n(n/s) (\nmy,sn,lfb\n;\n \nTauar\n-dict\n;\n \nTawer\n-mwb\n)\n \n–\n \ntower\n \n/ torre\n\n(\nEx/Ej(\nlfb7\n):\n \nBabel tawarka ba\n \n–\n \nThe tower of Babel\n \n/ La torre de babel)\n\nTaya\n \n(1) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nrelative\n \n(family relative),\n \ntribe\n \n/ pariente (familiar), tribu\n\n(\nC\nonstruct:\n \nTaiya\n;\n \nTamya\n;\n \nAi Taya\n \n(\na/t:\n \nTa\nika\n,\n \nTa\nyka\n)\n)\n\nTaya\n \n(2)\n \n(n\n/s\n)\n \n–\n \nleather\n, skin, hide,\n \nfish\n \nscale\ns\n, husk, feather\n, cover (of a book)\n \n/\n \ncuero, piel, escamas\n \nde pez\n, cáscara,\n\npluma, cubierta (de un libro)\n\n(Construct of skin (body part)\n \n/ Forma constructiva de piel (parte del cuerpo)\n:\n \nTai\nya\n;\n \nTam\nya\n;\n \nAi taya\n)\n\nDaiwan taya saika dadingkra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \ntanner\n \n/ curtidor\n\nDus\n \ntaya\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ntree bark\n \n/ corteza de arbol\n\nDus taya karbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto remove bark from a tree\n \n/ quitar la corteza de un arbol\n\nTaya klungwan\n \n(a/t:\n \nTaya klunhwan\n) (\ndb\n-\nIsa53:5\n)\n \n–\n \nflayed skin, cut skin, torn skin\n \n/ piel desollada, piel cortada,\n\npiel rasgada\n\nTaya pura\n \n(Alt:\n \nPura taya\n)\n \n–\n \nsurface\n, superficial\n \n/ superficie\n, superficial\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nwqu\n-\n09/19\n):\n \nDîa muni\n \nwiaia sip sa bawan l\nâ\nka ba pura taya baman sip marikras sa ki?\n \n–\n \nWhy are we able to say\n\nthat we\n \ncannot\n \nsee humility on the surface only?\n \n/ ¿Por qué podemos decir que no podemos ver la humildad solo en la\n\nsuperficie?\n)\n\nTaya sriwan\n \n–\n \nwrinkled skin\n \n/ piel arrugada\n\nTayat\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nbored, boring\n \n(\ntc\n), tired / aburrido, cansado\n\nTayat daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto bore, to make tired\n \n/ aburrir, hacer cansado\n\nTayat takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become bored, to become tired\n \n/ aburrirse, cansarse",
